---
title: ":butter: How to Cook Tofu"
author: Cooking For Peanuts
source: https://cookingforpeanuts.com/how-to-cook-tofu/
servings: 4
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
---

If using pre-pressed super-firm or extra-firm tofu, pat dry with paper towels. Otherwise, press the tofu for 10 to ~{15%minutes} and pat dry. Cut the @extra-firm tofu{16%oz} into cubes, planks, or triangles. Transfer to a medium #bowl{}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 375°F.

Make the marinade: In a small #bowl{}, whisk together the @low-sodium soy sauce{2%Tbsp} (or tamari), @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @nutritional yeast{2%Tbsp}, @water{1%Tbsp}, @sriracha{1.5%tsp} (optional), @olive oil{2%tsp} (or avocado oil), and @cornstarch{2%tsp} (or arrowroot). Adjust seasoning to taste.

Pour the marinade over the tofu and gently toss until evenly coated.

Oven-Bake: Line a rimmed #baking sheet{} with parchment paper or a silicone mat. Spread the tofu in an even layer with space between the pieces. Bake for ~{25%minutes}, flipping halfway through, until golden brown and crispy on the outside.

Air-Fryer Method (Alternative): Transfer marinated tofu to the basket of an #air fryer{} in a single layer. Air-fry at 375°F for 10 to ~{15%minutes}, shaking the basket halfway through, until crisp.

Pan-Fry Method (Alternative): Heat 1 to 2 tablespoons of oil in a non-stick #skillet{} over medium-high heat. Add the tofu in a single layer and cook for 8 to ~{10%minutes}, turning occasionally, until all sides are golden brown and crisp.

Serve warm in grain bowls, salads, veggie stir-fries, or wraps.
